+## Stage 03 implementation record — 21 September 2026
+
+The selected hybrid is implemented in `src/entry-public-server.tsx`, `src/entry-public-client.tsx`, `src/public/`, and `server/`. Both entries render the same `PublicPage` from the exact serialized snapshot; script state escapes `<` and Unicode line separators. Theme tokens, global/section renderers and CMS blocks have been extracted from their browser providers and are shared with the existing app. Product presentation reuses the storefront's product/gallery/purchase CSS and published presentation choice. No crawler-specific content or User-Agent branch exists.
+
+Rust `public_commerce::snapshot` owns the page/status envelope. `domain_catalog::public` projects explicit anonymous fields rather than serializing administrative products. Unknown/hidden/disabled attributes, media object keys, draft themes, unpublished CMS revisions and private customer context are excluded. Public attributes are currently scalar values with active visible definitions. Only primary image metadata is included in the initial projection; the existing interactive gallery/options remain in the shopper view.
+
+The initial response includes catalog base price for simple products. Configurable/grouped/bundle items invite option selection rather than suggesting the parent's numeric placeholder is a purchasable price. Availability is deliberately conservative: configured regional stores say availability varies by delivery location; non-regional stores still confirm stock during shopping. No InStock or personalized offer assertion is generated.
+
+Published theme product collections use bounded anonymous catalog queries, not personalized recommendation ranking. The existing live-search widget loads after hydration with its own query client; the server form works without JavaScript. Product purchase/options and personalized stock continue through a document navigation to `?shop=1`. This is an explicit transitional integration: inline cart/variant islands are not implemented. The meaningful product content never waits for that navigation or session restoration.
+
+Build from `frontend/apps/storefront` using the installed toolchain:
+
+```sh
+node ../../node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build
+node ../../node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build --ssr src/entry-public-server.tsx --outDir dist-server
+node server/seal-build.mjs
+```
+
+`build:publication` runs this sequence. Deploy `dist`, `dist-server`, server runtime and installed workspace dependencies from the same release. The seal records SHA-256 of the public template and SSR entry; startup rejects mismatches. Use Node 22.12+ with `NODE_ENV=production`. `PUBLICATION_APPROVED_ORIGIN`, `PUBLICATION_INSTALLATION_ID`, `PUBLICATION_GATEWAY`, `PUBLICATION_ARTIFACT_DIR`, `PUBLICATION_SSR_ENTRY`, `PUBLICATION_PORT` and `PUBLICATION_BIND` govern the runtime. Defaults bind localhost:8081 and fixed gateway localhost:8080. `/health` is process liveness; `/ready` validates a live snapshot/binding/schema and artifact validity is checked at startup.
+
+`compose.publication.yaml` adds an opt-in Node 22 renderer, read-only release mount and localhost-only port. `deploy/ec2/publication.py --host <approved-host> --gateway-port <port> --renderer-port <port>` sends merchant documents to Node and APIs to Rust. Keep PUBLICATION_NOINDEX=true through installation-specific rollout checks. No deployment was performed in Stage 03. Do not apply the overlay to demo/admin services.
+
+Local evidence uses real PostgreSQL and the Rust gateway, production-built Vite entries, curl, Chromium with and without JavaScript, an assigned published theme distinct from its draft, and a second installation with overlapping catalog identifiers. Full merchant-theme screenshot parity across every published theme and a deployed TLS/CDN response remain separate rollout checks; local screenshots are retained as fixtures, not production screenshots.
